00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:14.983
"Imara," the word
means power in Swahili.

00:00:14.983 --> 00:00:16.900
It is also the name of
an outreach effort that

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.510
has begun at the Massachusetts
Institute of Technology's

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:22.716
Computer Science and Artificial
Intelligence Laboratory.

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:31.080
CSAIL is an
interdepartmental laboratory

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.330
that includes faculty from
electrical engineering

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:37.410
and computer science, mechanical
engineering, mathematics, brain

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:41.030
and cognitive science,
aeronautics and astronautics,

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:44.070
the Biological Engineering
division, and the Harvard MIT

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:46.920
division of Health
Sciences and Technology.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.860
CSAIL is also the home of
the Worldwide Web Consortium.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:03.230
Our goal is to find
innovative ways

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:05.690
to enable domestic and
international communities

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:08.510
through a combination of
education and technology,

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:11.210
resources to which these
communities might not otherwise

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:13.160
have access.

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:17.600
Technology by itself is only
a tool, a means to an end.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.030
But as history has shown,
access to the proper tools

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:22.780
can vastly improve
the quality of life.

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:25.700
Imara looks for opportunities
to provide communities

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:28.400
with the tools of
computation and communication

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.120
and to enrich these
with education.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:35.440
MIT and CSAIL provide the
technical expertise, logistics,

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:38.760
and educational
resources behind Imara.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:40.590
Our corporate and
philanthropic partners

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:42.360
provide funding and
equipment to help

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.820
meet each community's needs.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:47.250
Together with our partners,
we find innovative ways

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.020
to overcome the
myriad challenges

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:51.150
of remote and
underserved populations.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:02.640
We believe in solving problems
that the community prioritizes,

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:06.110
not pushing Western
ideals and values.

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:08.990
To this end, we work
closely with local experts

00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:13.270
in each community to understand
their needs and values.

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.340
The underlying
philosophy of Imara

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:19.180
is to enable, not to just hand
out computers to the poor,

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:21.070
but to teach them
how to use technology

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:23.590
to improve their lives
and then in turn give

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:27.130
the gift of knowledge to
other neighboring communities.

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:30.160
We help keep this
self-sufficient cycle in motion

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.410
through longitudinal
outcome studies

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:34.460
and learn from our
successes and our failures

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:37.580
so we can continuously
improve our efforts.

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.490
Since Imara is a
volunteer organization,

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:44.240
we are in constant need of
computing and network equipment

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:47.470
as well as funding for
administration and travel.

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:49.930
Your organization can
play a role in Imara

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:52.600
by contacting our
outreach coordinator

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:56.410
at the email address or phone
number shown on your screen.

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:58.260
Thank you.

